Heroes! ⚔️

The winds of change are howling as the current season comes to an end: the Winter is coming... soon. But our update is coming now! And with it, we're bringing some welcome changes along to cheer you up and get us all prepared for the Winter holidays.

{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/28289343/546b39ea6ace79dfffe42e3b52c3029620cb4ff3.png

Let's hesitate no longer. We invite you to review the changes that you can expect to see in this, the November 2021 update.

⭐General changes:
- The Shop is expanding with a new offer of Monthly Cards — an updated format of subscriptions and a new way to get a stable income of gems that we will be rolling out over time. Activate it once for a whole month, get an instant reward and watch those chests get fuller and fuller of that shiny green stuff every day!
- New Divine Arenas have been added to the current rotation;
- Performed visual touch-ups throughout the game: in rewards, hero overview for Order faction and event roadmap.

⭐Bug fixes and minor enhancements:
- Improved readability in Daily, Weekly and Epic quests;
- Fixed visual glitches in battles — healing effects now act a little more tame;
- Fixed a visual bug with event boss attempts;
- Fixed a bug that led to "Server Error 702" appearing for players returning to the game after a long break;
- Fixed a bug with victories not giving Fame;
- Fixed issues in texts and translations.

We're excited about the future changes we're cooking up. Stay tuned to our announcements to be among the first to know what the Winter holidays have in store for Mighty Party.

Heroes! 🛠️ 

Once a year, fear and terror envelop Pangea like a haunting fog. On these days, children are not allowed outside, and heroes sit in taverns, trying to drown their bad thoughts in booze. Very soon Halloween begins…
You may be heartsick for the most mystical night of the year, but you don't have to worry about our game.

Here's what's waiting for you and what we've fixed.

General changes: 

- New Halloween holiday decorations;
- Added new window announcing the event;
- Added new "Happy Halloween!" event, which will begin on October 22;
- Added new visual effects.

Bug fixes and gameplay improvements:

- Fixed bugs on iPhone 13;
- Fixed cache cleanup issues when updating web versions of the game;
- Fixed bugs during tutorials;
- Fixed visual issues in the Shop;
- Fixed visual issues during combat;
- Other minor visual issues have been fixed;
- Localization issues have been fixed.

Stay tuned! And...have a fun Halloween!

{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/28289343/061cb550bf7e4116f9bb7be2095db2cb45cab7aa.png

Heroes! 🛠️ 

In today's update, we've added a lot of visual changes to the game, as well as a number of fixes and improvements. The new shop window stands out among all the innovations! 

General changes: 

- The Shop window has been completely changed! Here you will find brisk trade, many new tempting offers, and truly legendary heroes!;
- A new epic quest to join Discord has been added;
- Added new visuals for events — each event will now feature its own unique design and Runes;
- Added new effects for heroes during battles. The battles will become even more exciting and memorable!
- Small visual improvements have been made to the icons in the squad, event, and the main screen;

Bug fixes and gameplay improvements: 

- Fixed a bug with disappearing attempts in the Dark Tower;
- Minor visual bug fixes;
- Localization bugs fixed.

Stay tuned!

{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/28289343/c8fec73579fa2bec48d0cfae807f943dfa5e6524.png

Heroes! 🍂

The tables are overflowing with festive food, the musicians are playing their hearts out, the dancers are b in unison, and joyful laughter is coming from all sides. Join the Harvest Festival!

We've got a special schedule and lots of presents for you during these fall days! 

- No holiday is complete without a Wish Shop, which will be available from September 3 to 6;
- From September 6 to 13 a special Celebration Pit will be available, and you will meet the most fearsome creatures of Pangea;
- From September 7 to 9 we've prepared Special Offers for the most active players!
- From September 10 to 16 there will be an event "Horn of Plenty" with a New Hero - Mosura Wind Breath!
- From September 15 to 17 the gates of the Special Divine Arena will open;
- From September 17 to 20 you'll be able to collect a fortune and have gems added to your coffers for taking part in the High Growth fable;
- From September 20 to 23 you'll be able to use the Festive Summon to join your squad with new and beloved heroes.

🌟Take a seat, invite your friends, and get in on the Harvest Festival!

{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/28289343/9806ac61dc465093862dd1786d63732a3107428c.png

Heroes! 🛠

The Harvest Festival is starting on September 3, and the current update has created a special holiday atmosphere for you!
But first things first. Today, we’d like to tell you about the changes and bug fixes that you’ll see in this update.

General changes: 

- Completely updated the event window, taking into account the feedback from players! This is very important for us. We made huge changes in visual presentation of events, so you can fully enjoy the gameplay and catch every detail of the plot!
- Removed the ability to subscribe in the game. All active subscriptions will not be affected and their owners will receive their rewards on time. Terms and conditions of automatic renewal of active subscriptions remain unchanged. But don't despair, there will be something new to replace subscriptions!
- Added a new event, "Horn of Plenty" that will start September 10; 
- Added new epic quests, asking you to subscribe to our social networks. Stay tuned and get rewarded;
- Changed home and loading screen designs for the Harvest Festival.

Bug fixes and gameplay improvements: 

- Fixed the incorrect work of the first skill for Grace of Rockfleet;
- Fixed a bug with the disappearance of the first purchase reward;
- Fixed errors related to the completion of the Mighty Pass;
- Fixed issues occurring in the Guild window and during Turf Wars;
- Fixed visual bugs in Special Offers and Deals;
- Fixed timer bugs in Deals;
- Fixed bugs in the Daily Rewards window.

Stay tuned!

{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/28289343/fbe9d88b8644905e6b6477cf6169209d2b96f9a7.jpg

🌴 Heroes! Oh, it's so hot! 🌴

Time to pull out your favorite shorts and shirt, head to the lounge chair and enjoy the Summer Festival in Mighty Party!

Catch a wave, defeat the Bosses in the Pit, leisurely sip tropical drinks, and immerse yourself in this epic celebration in the company of a new hero, Grace of Rockfleet!

On these sunny days, we've prepared a special schedule for you: 
- From July 19 to 22 you'll have access to everyone's favorite Combat Packs;
- From July 23 to 26 you'll be able to collect a fortune and have gems added to your coffers for participating in High Growth;
- From July 26 to August 2 a special Celebration Pit will be available, and you'll meet some of Pangea's most fearsome creatures;
- From July 27 to 30 your squad with be joined by new and beloved heroes with the help of Festive Summon;
- From July 30 to August 5 a new and unforgettable event with new hero awaits you! 
- From August 2 to 4 we've prepared Special Offers for the most active players!
- From August 4 to 6 the Divine Arena will open its gates;
- And, of course, no holiday can go without our Wish Shop, which will be available from August 6 to 8;

And for the most attentive and those who want to enjoy the holiday to the fullest, we will prepare a promo code and post it on our Facebook page. Follow the news and stay tuned!

Don't wait for too long. Like any vacation, Summer Festival will be over before you know it!

{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/28289343/11635fba3697bfd652cca5825258aa92b6a393a1.png

Heroes! 🛠 

The most attentive players may have noticed that in the previous update description we mentioned a change to the "High Growth" fable, namely: "The quest requirements of the High Growth fable have been adapted to increase the card drop. Players will be able to increase the level of cards more often, so the number of Gems for completing these quests will not decrease".

You may have noted that the last "High Growth" fable went unchanged, while the number and quality of cards obtained in the prizes and chests increased several times back on 06.01.2021

We hope you enjoyed taking part in this event, but unfortunately for the sake of resource and card balancing the change will come into effect.

As of July 23, the balance of the "High Growth" fable timeline will be altered so that more heroes will be required to complete each step of the timeline.

At the same time, the Rich Gifts and Desired Wealth fables that go along with "High Growth" will remain unchanged.

⭐ General changes:
- Changed the balance of the "High Growth" fable;
- Updated the design of the quest window.

⭐ Bugs Fixes: 
- Fixed a bug with incorrect display of captured cell owner in Turf War;
- Fixed a bug with missing progress;
- Fixed incorrect display of the number of souls received from the Journey Chest;
- Fixed a bug with the appearance of offers with sparks after the end of the Event;
- Fixed a bug with counting Battle Pass chests in Event quests;
- Fixed other minor and visual bugs.

Stay tuned!

{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/28289343/c8fec73579fa2bec48d0cfae807f943dfa5e6524.png

Heroes! 🛠

Following the balance update, we have added several innovations and fixed some bugs so that you could enjoy the game!

⭐Main changes:

- We’ve made a completely new notification window. You can adjust notifications in a way convenient for you. It’s easier now to stay informed about game news;
- We’ve rebalanced the Gold Mine. Now the level of this mode depends on your progress in the Journey. The more you achieve in the Journey, the more gold you will get in the Gold Mine;
- Hunting is now available during events! At any time you can make your faithful pets stronger and start an exciting Adventure with them!

⭐Bugs fixes:

- Fixed a bug with disappearing events;
- Fixed a bug with the appearance of event offers in the store after its end;
- Fixed localization bugs caused by various combinations of the game's and system's languages;
- Fixed a bug with disappearance of several attempts in the Dark Tower when a player is defeated;
- Fixed a bug with the game freezing when windows are switched too fast;

Stay tuned!

{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/28289343/8dcd07e666d6e0da4d2d2205cffa72198bb46bd6.png

Heroes! Future update! 🛠

The fourth birthday of Mighty Party has noisily taken place just recently. And although the sounds of horns and the songs of the bards have ceased, that's no reason to lay down your arms.
This update will be the biggest balance change in the history of Mighty Party. We've redesigned the rewards in most game modes, and players will now receive many more cards. The purpose of these changes is to freshen up the gameplay and make players' progress more dynamic.

So, for example, players will now receive epic and legendary cards in the Divine Arena, in the free lineup of the Battle Pass, and from other sources, where previously only rare and epic cards were dropped. In addition, the usual rewards have also been increased: the chances to get epic and legendary cards in the summons are now higher, and the very number of souls has increased significantly. In the end-of-season reward, players will be able to receive up to 2,000 legendary cards!

In order to balance and adapt the game for these changes, we are making several important innovations. First of all, we will change the recommended might in the Hall of Fame and redistribute players by league to make the game interesting and leave room for development. The leagues of most players will be lower, but there's no reason to be sad about it because in the end the rewards will be significantly increased and it will be easier to progress through the leagues. This change will not affect players in the top 200 rankings at the time of the update, but their Fame will be reset to 15,000.

Here is the full list of changes in this update:

- Rewards are increased in all summons. There is only one guaranteed legendary card in the Demigods x10 summon, but the total value of the summon will be much greater;
- Only legendary cards in the summon of Gods;
Significantly increased rewards in the Battle Pass, added legendary cards to the Free Access (to see changes, wait until the start of the new Battle Pass);
- Trophy rewards increased;
- The quest requirements of the High Growth fable have been adapted to increase the card drop. Players will be able to increase the level of cards more often, so the number of Gems for completing these quests will not decrease;
- Starting with League 20, the minimum reward for winning in the - - Hall of Fame will be a rare chest;
- The drop chance of the legendary chests has been significantly increased, and you can now get them in the League 19;
- Starting with League 20, the time to open chests has been significantly reduced (up to 66% faster);
- Now, starting with League 20, the victory chest will become rare instead of common;
- Rewards for League promotion have been increased. Starting with - League 17, you will be able to get legendary chests;
- End-of-season rewards have been increased. Legendary chests will also be available starting with League 17;
- Significantly increased rewards in game sets from the "Deals" menu;
- You can buy cards of legendary and epic heroes the moment the Black Market updates at 18:00 UTC or the moment an update with the help of VIP takes place;
- Increased the maximum level available for heroes in Leagues;
- The amount of soul dust obtained by sacrificing heroes is adapted to the increased drop of cards;
- You can get epic chests as a reward in the Divine Arena, and on major holidays you can get legendary ones;
- Increased rewards for daily and weekly quests;
- Gems are added to rewards for weekly quests;
- Significantly increased the reward in the legendary chest for disciples who reach League 17;
- Changed the balance of issuing Copper Coins in the Pit;
- Buying Copper Coins for Gems has become much more profitable.

Stay tuned!

{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/28289343/00217b3fa2994359c53d7aa049fe5a3792d9ef2d.png

Heroes! 
Mighty Party Festive Update is now available! 

We are already in full swing preparing for an incredible birthday celebration, but we remember about your wishes as well. In this update, we have tried to fix most of the annoying bugs and added some simple but pleasant innovations.

General changes: 

- Added a festive decoration;
- Updated the Gems Mine window;
- Updated the window to speed up the opening of chests;
- Now chests given at the end of the season are counted in event quests.

Bug fixes:

- Fixed a bug with counting number of attempts in modes when VIP status is active;
- Fixed animation bug of receiving a reward for purchasing an extra slot;
- Fixed a bug with authorization via Facebook on IOS;
- Fixed the disappearance of quests during the hunt.

Stay tuned!

{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/28289343/c8fec73579fa2bec48d0cfae807f943dfa5e6524.png

Heroes! 

Mighty Party Festive Update! 

Our team works tirelessly so that every event or innovation can please you. We strive to make your time spent in the game as enjoyable and exciting as possible, so that you can have fun every day and share your emotions with your friends!

Therefore, we are glad to share with you the innovations of the fresh update:

- Easter cannot do without festive decoration, so we have updated the main and loading screens;
- Added a new medal for completing the Easter event;
- In the next event you can add a new hero to your squad;
- Now, when you first install the application on the device, the language of your system will be selected! You can manually change the language through the settings menu or directly on the boot screen;
- The settings window has been transformed and received a new design, and a new convenient menu has appeared on the loading screen;

In this update, many minor but annoying bugs were fixed, as well as localization flaws.
Of course, we paid special attention to more serious bugs:

- We have changed the matchmaking in the Dark Tower;
- In addition, we have worked on the selection of opponents in Rating Matches;
- Fixed incorrect accrual of experience in Journey;
- Fixed visual bugs in the Dark Tower;
- Fixed a bug with the background disappearance in events;
- Tamed the “jumping” event icon on the main screen;
- Fixed all the problems related to the chest in Journey;
- Returned the gallery to the players who lost it;
- Fixed notification for epic quests.

Thanks to the players and their feedback, we can develop Mighty Party in the right direction and get better every day!
Thank you for showing patience and understanding when needed.

Best regards, Mighty Party team.

{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/28289343/c8fec73579fa2bec48d0cfae807f943dfa5e6524.png

Heroes! 
The Update is now available!

General changes:
- Improved optimization and loading speed of the game;
- Removed the cooldown between the end of a Battle Pass and the start of a new one;
- Changed rank progression;
- Reduced time for updating attempts in an event from 6 to 2 hours;
- Changed gaining experience from the Journey chest;
- Added a feature that allows to gain experience for completing Journey stages;
- Added indication for trophies in the Journey mode, a chest with rewards, and the Gems Fund;
- Added indication for Pit and Dark Tower to the main screen;
- Changed the graphical display of attempts in the Pit and Dark Tower in the VIP section;
- Fixed localization errors;
- Removed New Year's decoration.

Bug fixes:
- Fixed a bug with the game freezing when opening the list of guild members;
- Fixed a bug with displaying resources on the main screen;
- Fixed a bug with multiple pressing of the "collect" and "x2" buttons near the Journey chest;
- Fixed a bug with lack of animation for buttons.

{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/28289343/fbe9d88b8644905e6b6477cf6169209d2b96f9a7.jpg

Heroes!

The New Year is approaching. It is cold and snowy outside, frost draws patterns on the windows, and you are probably already sitting by the fireplace, wrapped in a blanket, and enjoying the next fight.

We would like the coming year to delight you with pleasant surprises, good meetings, and hot battles!

Before that, we want to please you with another update:

The Update is now available!

General changes:
- Completely changed main screen design;
- Added New Year's decoration;
- Improved game optimization.

Bug fixes:
- Fixed bug with incorrect display of the number of boss attempts in events;
- Fixed bug with displaying purchase of Gems Fund in the guild chat;
- Fixed bug with notification about restoration of attempts in Journey;
- Changed display of the price of the Gems Fund;
- Fixed display of the "block" skill in Journey;
- Fixed bugs when buying a subscription;
- Fixed localization bugs.

The Update for WEB, Android and Steam is now available!

Bug fixes:
- Removed global chat notification;
- Fixed display of daily reward;
- Fixed bug with receiving daily rewards;
- Fixed display of portraits;
- Fixed bugs with scrolling through lots in the Shop;
- Fixed other minor bugs.

Please update the game for the changes to take effect.
Bug fixes on IOS platform are expected as soon as possible.

{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/28289343/05546cbac29483d94f82bea7082d64fd57bcd970.jpg

Heroes! ⚔️

The Update is now available!

🛠 General changes:
- Changed weekly offers in the store;
- The difficulty of some Journey bosses has been changed from Chapter 4 to Chapter 8.
- Added Gems Fund
The Gems Fund is a temporary offer that will expire when the timer expires (14 days). After purchasing the Gems Fund, you can get additional gems for unlimited time for completing bosses in Journey

🛠 Bug fixes:
- Fixed a bug with the number of daily and weekly rewards;
- Now rewards from trophies are counted in event nodes;
- Fixed a bug with doubling the heroes of the event when receiving them from the Chest with gifts;
- Event sparks have been added to the Devine Arena;
- Fixed display of friends on the Journey map;
- Fixed bugs when buying a subscription;
- Fixed display of awards in the Pit;
- Fixed incorrect work of rewards for disciples purchases;
- Fixed incorrect operation of purchasing premium trophies when completing a sector;
- Fixed a bug with repeating the ""First Blood"" event;
- Fixed incorrect display of fonts;
- Fixed localization bugs;
- Fixed a bug with displaying cards requested by friends.

{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/28289343/f9516609a2d522b31fbbcb4e98e15387c33cd904.png

Heroes!

It's time to go on an epic adventure!
Get ready to fight many opponents, get valuable rewards and, of course, take a fresh look at your favorite regime!

General changes:
- Added new Journey battlegrounds;
- Updated  key characters' art;
- Introduced new game mechanics with puzzles, which will appeal to all strategists and help diversify the battles in the world of Pangea!
- Changed rewards in Dark Tower, The Pit and Raids;
- Changed the cost of lots in the "Black Market";
- Changed all quests concerning "Ancient coins" with regard to the new currency "Copper coins";
- "Ancient coins" will be converted into gems;

Reward for play time:
- Added rewards for the time spent in the game;
- Rewards will be generated daily;
- Quantity of rewards depends on the current League;

Journey Mode:
- At the time of the update, 3 islands divided into 9 sectors will be available, but in the future we plan to add even more new locations!
- On the sector map you'll be able to see the progress of your friends, get ready for a boss fight, of course open the treasure chest and get the Trophies!
- Each sector will contain at least 30 levels with rewards for completion;
- Every 5 levels  you will face a boss that is essential to the story on your way;
- Levels, Bosses, Sectors and Islands as a whole cannot be completed again;
- For the battle, you no longer need the attempts, so you can try to complete the levels an unlimited number of times, but you will not be able to replay the level or get rewards several times;
- Attempts will be required to complete event bosses;
- A reward chest that will be gradually filled with special rewards will be added to Journey;
- The chest will fill up to its maximum in 12 hours.
- The rewards of the chest increase after completion of every 5 levels;

Trophies:
- Each sector will offer additional rewards in the form of Trophies;
- You can get them if you manage to complete the levels within a certain time;
- You can get even more rewards by activating Premium;
- When moving to a new sector, you will not be able to  receive Trophies from the previous one. So hurry up to get them on time!
- The trophies of each sector have a timer, after which, the trophies that you did not manage to open will not be available (including Premium trophies).
- The number of trophies increases with each subsequent sector.
- If you didn't manage to get the trophies on time, then you can activate Premium and get those trophies that you managed to open during the timer.

Reworking Journey would impossible without revealing the story  of Adam and his companions, so in the mode you'll find:

- New arts of Adam, Lilith, Agasfer, and Minstrel;
- Reworked main plot;
- Updated dialog window;
- New heroes to the story.

{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/28289343/f9516609a2d522b31fbbcb4e98e15387c33cd904.png

{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/28289343/f9516609a2d522b31fbbcb4e98e15387c33cd904.png

Heroes!

The Update is now available!

Bugs were fixed with the update:

- Visual improvements;
- Animation improvements;
- Buddhist calendar bug fixed;
- Freeze bug on opponent's turn has been fixed;
- Max Rank has been increased to 2000;
- Soul Dust cannot be found in Win Chests any longer;
- Fixed bug with double boost heroes;
- Fixed a bug with the number of friends;
- Now the maximum number of friends depends on the league, not on the rank;
- Attack and HP of heroes has been changed.

You can read more about the changes in the characteristics of the heroes in the patchout, on our Facebook page! 
https://www.facebook.com/notes/mighty-party/patch-notes-from-30032020/1301167350053817/

Heroes!

New update is available!

Hero Skill Changes:

1) Ghosta;
2) Stormrage;
3) Shao Lin;
4) Tani Windrunner;
5) Olaf the Red;
6) Demon Huntress;
7) Drow.

From now on, instead of killing enemies instantly, Heroes will deal a significant amount of damage capable to decrease most heroes' HP down to ZERO. It applies to the heroes with the same rarity and level (including Reborn and Soulbound ones).   

Reward Changes:

1) For the older players (playing experience is over 4 months) from League 30 to League 8 all the PvP rewards and goods from the season chests will be reduced.

2) For the newcomers (playing experience is less than 4 months) from League 7 to League GM these rewards and lots will be increased.

Friendship Gifts:

1) From now on you won't be able to send any epic heroes to your friends.

2) Instead, you'll be able to receive enough rare cards from your friends to Evolve them into some epic heroes all by yourself.
 
Gold-giving mechanics changes:

We've revised the gold-giving mechanics for PvP victories. This includes: Win Streak Bonuses, Guild Bonuses and VIP Bonuses.

Quest System Revised:

1) The Path of Hero was deleted from the game;

2) A new 10-part quest chain was added;

3) Daily Quests revised;

4) Weekly Quests added;

5) Epic Quests revised:
  
  - Quests which involve collecting 2-, 3-, 5-star Heroes were deleted;
  - Skin-related victories were deleted;
  - Guild activity quests were added;
  - The Hunt quests were added;
  - The Pit victory quests were added;
  - Evolve-related quests were fixed;
  - Divine Arena victory quests were added;
  - VIP-related quests were added;
  - The Dark Tower victory quests were added;
  - The Journey mode's quest balance was fixed.

Bugs fixing:

1) Prince Gleedy's third active skill has been fixed;

2) Sudden Death's bug fixing;

3) Immunity's bug fixing.https://steamcdn-a.akamaihd.net/steamcommunity/public/images/clans/28289343/45178244d94e685c1bf66ff93ac6df284edaf9f4.jpg

